.\" -*- coding: UTF-8 -*-
.TH SEGLCD-GTK 1 "2026-11-20" "seglcd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
seglcd-gtk \- graphical settings for the SegLcd service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B seglcd-gtk
.RB [ \-\-system | \-\-session ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B seglcd-gtk
connects to
.BR seglcdd (1)
over D-Bus, shows the display state and the current values, and sets the intervals and the sensor of each value.
Changes apply at once;
.B Save
makes them permanent (D-Bus SaveConfig), the reload button discards unsaved changes.
.PP
It looks for the system service first, then for the user service, and reconnects when the service restarts.
Controlling the system service requires membership in the group
.BR seglcd .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-system
Only use the system service (system bus).
.TP
.B \-\-session
Only use the user service (session bus).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for invalid arguments, 3 if no display can be opened.
.SH TRADEMARKS
SegLcd is an independent project and not affiliated with Thermaltake. Thermaltake is a trademark of Thermaltake Technology Co., Ltd.; the name is used only to identify the supported hardware.
.SH SEE ALSO
